With a non-zero letter-spacing, Ladybird turns off liga, clig, dlig, and
hlig, except for a feature that font-feature-settings set. Gecko does
the same: gfxFontShaper::MergeFontFeatures() turns those four off for
its aDisableLigatures, which a non-zero letter-spacing sets, and lets
font-feature-settings override them. Blink’s FontFeatures::Initialize()
turns off liga, clig, and calt, and leaves dlig and hlig off, whenever
the FontDescription’s LetterSpacing() isn’t zero.

In Chrome 157 and Firefox 151, “office affix” in M+ 1p with 20px of
letter-spacing took the spacing 12 times by default, with common-
ligatures, and with discretionary-ligatures; 7 times when font-feature-
settings turned liga on; and 12 times when it turned liga off. Ladybird
now does the same, where before it took the spacing 7 times in all but
the last case. Armenian text that a system fallback font draws behaves
the same way in all three.
